In .NET 10 (starting with .NET 10 Preview 4), `WindowSoftInputModeAdjust.Resize` was deprecated because Android itself deprecated the underlying `adjustResize` mode. The replacement is the **edge-to-edge** layout model with `KeyboardAcceleratorsPlacement` and the new `ImeInsets` API.

Here's the recommended approach:

### 1. Enable edge-to-edge (Android)

In your `MainActivity.cs` or via platform config:

```csharp
// Platforms/Android/MainActivity.cs
protected override void OnCreate(Bundle? savedInstanceState)
{
    base.OnCreate(savedInstanceState);
    WindowCompat.SetDecorFitsSystemWindows(Window, false);
}
```

### 2. Use `Padding` bound to keyboard insets

In your page or view, subscribe to keyboard inset changes. .NET 10 adds `SafeAreaPadding` support that accounts for the IME:

```xml
<ContentPage xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml">
    <Grid Padding="{OnPlatform Android={x:Static Maui:SafeArea.Padding}}">
        <!-- Chat messages -->
        <CollectionView Grid.Row="0" ... />

        <!-- Input bar at bottom -->
        <HorizontalStackLayout Grid.Row="1">
            <Entry Placeholder="Type a message..." HorizontalOptions="FillAndExpand"/>
            <Button Text="Send"/>
        </HorizontalStackLayout>
    </Grid>
</ContentPage>
```

### 3. Alternative: handle insets manually via platform code

```csharp
// Platforms/Android/MainActivity.cs
ViewCompat.SetOnApplyWindowInsetsListener(Window.DecorView, (view, insets) =>
{
    var imeInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime());
    var navInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.NavigationBars());

    // Notify your page of the bottom inset
    var bottomPadding = Math.Max(imeInsets.Bottom, navInsets.Bottom)
                        / DeviceDisplay.MainDisplayInfo.Density;

    MessagingCenter.Send<object, double>(this, "KeyboardInset", bottomPadding);
    return ViewCompat.OnApplyWindowInsets(view, insets);
});
```

Then in your page:

```csharp
MessagingCenter.Subscribe<object, double>(this, "KeyboardInset", (_, bottom) =>
{
    MainThread.BeginInvokeOnMainThread(() => InputBar.Margin = new Thickness(0, 0, 0, bottom));
});
```

### Summary

| .NET 9 | .NET 10 |
|--------|---------|
| `WindowSoftInputModeAdjust.Resize` | Edge-to-edge + IME window insets |

The key shift is from the old "resize the window" model to "listen for inset changes and adjust padding/margin yourself," which matches modern Android (API 30+) behavior.
